Temperatures in the northern part of Nigeria can go as high as 48 ° C ( 118.4 ° F ) in cities like Maiduguri . The high temperatures coupled with an increase in insolation causes a region of low pressure to develop over west Africa and Nigeria ( between March to May ) . The Tropical continental airmass ( CT ) from the Sahara Desert in the northern part of West Africa , is weakened due to the overheating of the land surface in west Africa and Nigeria at this time . The Tropical continental airmass ( CT ) begins to retreat northwards to the Sahara Desert due to massive heating of the land which transfers heat in the form of convection into the Tropical continental airmass ( CT ) which constitutes the main layer of air above the land . This transfer of heat in the Tropical continental airmass ( CT ) in turn , causes the wind to expand and become lighter as this is the normal behaviour for winds moving above intensely heated grounds .","entities":["northern part of Nigeria","West Africa","Maiduguri","Sahara Desert","low pressure","wind","convection","Tropical Continental Airmass","Nigeria"],"facts":["West Africa -RELATED_TO-> temperature","Sahel climate -RELATED_TO-> northern part of Nigeria","low pressure region -LOCATED_IN-> West Africa","West Africa -RELATED_TO-> insolation","Intertropical Convergence Zone -RELATED_TO-> West Africa"]}
