version 3.3. 1 Charts 3.4 Selena version 3.5 Other versions 4 Soundtrack appearances 5 Legacy 6 References 7 External links Weekly charts ( edit ) Chart ( 1961 -- 63 ) Peak position Australia ( Kent Music Report ) Canada ( RPM ) Germany ( Official German Charts ) Japan ( Music Life ) Norway ( VG - lista ) UK Singles ( Official Charts Company ) 6 US Billboard Hot 100 US Adult Contemporary ( Billboard ) Lyrics ( edit ) The lyrics tell the story of a man who looks up and whistles while he is walking so that his tears will not fall . The verses of the song describe his memories and feelings . Rokusuke Ei wrote this song while coming back from a protest against the Treaty of Mutual Cooperation and Security between the United States and Japan and feeling dejected about the failure of the protest movement , but the lyrics were rendered purposefully generic so that they might refer to any lost love . The English - language lyrics of the version recorded by A Taste of Honey are not a translation of the original Japanese lyrics , but instead a completely different set of lyrics arranged to the same basic melody .","entities":["Rokusuke Ei","protest against the Treaty of Mutual Cooperation and Security between the United States and Japan","Treaty of Mutual Cooperation and Security between the United States and Japan","A Taste of Honey","Selena","United States","Japan","English","Japanese","Sukiyaki"],"facts":["A Taste of Honey -CREATED-> Sukiyaki (A Taste of Honey version)","A Taste of Honey -CREATED-> A Taste of Honey's version of Sukiyaki","A Taste of Honey -RELATED_TO-> Boogie Oogie Oogie","A Taste of Honey -RELATED_TO-> Sukiyaki by A Taste of Honey on Soul Train","Billboard Hot Soul Singles number-one single (A Taste of Honey version) -PARTICIPATED_IN-> A Taste of Honey"]}
