and min . temperatures in ° C Precipitation totals in mm History Main article : History of Hawaii Part of a series on the History of Hawaii Timeline Ancient Kingdom of Hawaii Provisional Government Republic of Hawaii Modern - day Hawaii U.S. Territory State of Hawaii Hawaii portal Hawaii is one of four U.S. states -- apart from the original thirteen , along with the Vermont Republic ( 1791 ) , the Republic of Texas ( 1845 ) , and the California Republic ( 1846 ) -- that were independent nations prior to statehood . Along with Texas , Hawaii had formal , international diplomatic recognition as a nation . The Kingdom of Hawai ʻi was sovereign from 1810 until 1893 when the monarchy was overthrown by resident American and European capitalists and landholders . Hawaii was an independent republic from 1894 until August 12 , 1898 , when it officially became a territory of the United States . Hawaii was admitted as a U.S. state on August 21 , 1959 .","entities":["Republic of Hawaii","Vermont Republic","Republic of Texas","California Republic","Texas","Overthrow of the monarchy","Hawaii became a territory of the United States","Hawaii admitted as a U.S. state","Kingdom of Hawaiʻi","Hawaii","United States"],"facts":["annexation -RELATED_TO-> Republic of Hawaii","ʻIolani Palace -RELATED_TO-> Republic of Hawaii","Republic of Hawaii -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Annexation of the Republic of Hawaii","Sanford B. Dole -WORKS_FOR-> Republic of Hawaii","House of Kamehameha -RELATED_TO-> Kingdom of Hawaiʻi"]}
