The song , which has been described by members of Three Dog Night as a `` kid 's song '' and a `` silly song '' , topped the main singles charts in North America , was certified gold by the RIAA , and has since been covered by multiple artists . The song is featured prominently in the film The Big Chill . It is sung by a child character at the beginning and the Three Dog Night recording is played over the end credits . It is also played at the end of every Denver Broncos home victory . Notable playings of this song after Broncos victories included then - Chicago Bears head coach Abe Gibron 's singing along with the song in 1973 ; and at the end of Super Bowl XXXII , played at Qualcomm Stadium in San Diego . It was also played at the end of Super Bowl XXXIII at Pro Player ( now Hard Rock ) Stadium in Miami Gardens , Florida and Super Bowl 50 in Santa Clara , California . Contents ( hide ) 1 Background and recording 2 Charts and awards 3 In popular culture 4 References 5 External links Background and Recording ( edit ) Some of the words are nonsensical .","entities":["The Big Chill","RIAA","main singles charts","North America","Denver Broncos","Abe Gibron","Chicago Bears","Super Bowl XXXII","Qualcomm Stadium","San Diego","Super Bowl XXXIII","Pro Player Stadium","Miami Gardens","Florida","Super Bowl 50"],"facts":["Joy to the World -RELATED_TO-> Rock","Joy to the World -RELATED_TO-> Dunhill","Joy to the World -RELATED_TO-> I Can Hear You Calling","Joy to the World -RELATED_TO-> American Recording Co.","Joy to the World -RELATED_TO-> One Man Band"]}
