Adobe AIR was upgraded to support 64 - bit computers , and to allow developers to add additional functionality to the AIR runtime using AIR Native Extensions ( ANE ) . In 2014 , Adobe AIR reached a milestone with over 100,000 unique applications built , and over 1 billion installations logged across the world ( May 2014 ) . Adobe AIR was voted the Best Mobile Application Development product at the Consumer Electronics Show on two consecutive years ( CES 2014 and CES 2015 ) . In 2016 , Adobe renamed Flash Professional , the primary authoring software for Flash content , to Adobe Animate to reflect its growing use for authoring HTML5 content in favour of Flash content . Open Screen Project ( edit ) On May 1 , 2008 , Adobe announced the Open Screen Project , with the intent of providing a consistent application interface across devices such as personal computers , mobile devices , and consumer electronics .","entities":["Adobe Flash","Adobe AIR","Adobe","AIR Native Extensions","Best Mobile Application Development product","CES 2014","CES 2015","Adobe Animate","Open Screen Project announcement","Open Screen Project","HTML5","Flash content"],"facts":["FutureWave Software -CREATED-> Adobe Flash","Macromedia -CREATED-> Adobe Flash","Adobe Systems -CREATED-> Adobe Flash","Thibault Imbert -CREATED-> Adobe Flash","FutureWave -CREATED-> Adobe Flash"]}
{"title":"Adobe Flash","text":"Adobe Flash
Macromedia distributed Flash Player as a free browser plugin in order to quickly gain market share . By 2005 , more computers worldwide had Flash Player installed than any other Web media format , including Java , QuickTime , RealNetworks and Windows Media Player . Macromedia upgraded the Flash system between 1996 and 1999 adding MovieClips , Actions ( the precursor to ActionScript ) , Alpha transparency , and other features . As Flash matured , Macromedia 's focus shifted from marketing it as a graphics and media tool to promoting it as a Web application platform , adding scripting and data access capabilities to the player while attempting to retain its small footprint . In 2000 , the first major version of ActionScript was developed , and released with Flash 5 . Actionscript 2.0 was released with Flash MX 2004 and supported object - oriented programming , improved UI components and other programming features . The last version of Flash released by Macromedia was Flash 8 , which focused on graphical upgrades such as filters ( blur , drop shadow , etc . ) , blend modes ( similar to Adobe Photoshop ) , and advanced features for FLV video .","entities":["ActionScript","Flash 5","Macromedia","Flash","MovieClips","Actions","Alpha transparency","Java","QuickTime","RealNetworks","ActionScript 2.0","Flash MX 2004","object-oriented programming","UI components","Flash 8"],"facts":["ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> video games","ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> interactive animations","ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> web applications","ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> desktop applications","ActionScript -RELATED_TO-> Adobe Flash"]}

