The main reasons underlying this trend are that some Gulf Coast refiners have reduced Nigerian imports in favor of domestically - produced crude , and that two refineries in the U.S. East Coast , which were significant buyers of Nigerian crude , were idled in late 2011 . As a result , Nigerian crude as a share of total United States imports has fallen to 5 percent in the first half of 2012 , down from 10 and 11 percent in the first half of 2011 and 2010 , respectively , according to the International Energy Agency . According to the CIA World Factbook , Nigeria 's main export partners are the United States , India , Brazil , Spain , France and the Netherlands . Shell has been working in Nigeria since 1936 , and currently dominates gas production in the country , as the Niger Delta , which contains most of Nigeria 's gas resources , also houses most of Shell 's hydrocarbon assets . History and politics ( edit ) See also : History of Nigeria and Niger Delta An Ethno - linguistic map of Nigeria .","entities":["India","International Energy Agency","Gulf Coast","U.S. East Coast","Nigerian crude","CIA World Factbook","Brazil","the Netherlands","gas production","Shell's hydrocarbon assets","History of Nigeria","History and politics","Ethno-linguistic map of Nigeria","United States","Niger Delta"],"facts":["United States -RELATED_TO-> the war","Nigeria ceased exports to the US -RELATED_TO-> United States","India -RELATED_TO-> Nigerian oil","United States -RELATED_TO-> Nigeria government","Dean Rusk -RELATED_TO-> United States"]}
