The Black stallion ( film ) - wikipedia The Black stallion ( film ) Jump to : navigation , search The Black Stallion 1979 poster Directed by Carroll Ballard Produced by Fred Roos Francis Ford Coppola Tom Sternberg Screenplay by Melissa Mathison Jeanne Rosenberg William D. Wittliff Based on The Black Stallion by Walter Farley Starring Kelly Reno Mickey Rooney Teri Garr Music by Carmine Coppola Cinematography Caleb Deschanel Edited by Robert Dalva Production company American Zoetrope Distributed by United Artists Release date October 17 , 1979 ( 1979 - 10 - 17 ) Running time 118 minutes Country United States Language English Budget $2.7 million Box office $37.8 million The Black Stallion is a 1979 American adventure film based on the 1941 classic children 's novel The Black Stallion by Walter Farley . But the film starts in 1946 , five years after the book was published . It tells the story of Alec Ramsey , who is shipwrecked on a deserted island with a wild Arabian stallion whom he befriends .","entities":["The Black Stallion","Fred Roos","Tom Sternberg","Melissa Mathison","Jeanne Rosenberg","William D. Wittliff","Walter Farley","Kelly Reno","Mickey Rooney","Teri Garr","Caleb Deschanel","Robert Dalva","American Zoetrope","United Artists","United States"],"facts":["Mickey Rooney -RELATED_TO-> The Adventures of the Black Stallion","Teri Garr -RELATED_TO-> Mrs. Ramsay","Kelly Reno -RELATED_TO-> Alec Ramsay","Mickey Rooney -RELATED_TO-> Henry Dailey","United States National Film Registry -LOCATED_IN-> United States"]}
