London : Oxford University Press . p. 181 . ISBN 0 - 19 - 502216 - 5 . In fact , the woods are not , as the Lathem edition would have it ( with its obtuse emendation of a comma after the second adjective in line 13 ) , merely ' lovely , dark , and deep . ' Rather , as Frost in all the editions he supervised intended , they are ' lovely , ( i.e. ) dark and deep ' ; the loveliness thereby partakes of the depth and darkness which make the woods so ominous . Jump up ^ `` My Brush with History - `` We Heard the Shots ... '' : Aboard the Press Bus in Dallas 40 Years Ago '' ( PDF ) . Archived from the original on 26 September 2012 . Retrieved 2013 - 06 - 30 . CS1 maint : BOT : original - url status unknown ( link ) Jump up ^ Davis , Sid ; Bennett , Susan ; Trost , Catherine ' Cathy ' ; Rather , Daniel ' Dan ' Irvin Jr ( 2004 ) . `` Return To The White House '' .","entities":["Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening","Sid Davis","London","Oxford University Press","Frost","Lathem edition","My Brush with History - We Heard the Shots ... : Aboard the Press Bus in Dallas 40 Years Ago","Dallas","Susan Bennett","Catherine Trost","Daniel Irvin Jr","Return To The White House"],"facts":["Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening -PART_OF-> New Hampshire","Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening -RELATED_TO-> iambic tetrameter","Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening -RELATED_TO-> Rubaiyat stanza","Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening -RELATED_TO-> AABA - BBCB - CCDC - DDDD","Robert Frost -CREATED-> Stopping by Woods on a Snowy Evening"]}
