He is dethroned by the spectre of an actor , and we shall never be able to keep the usurper out of our dreams . Maurice Maeterlinck in La Jeune Belgique ( 1890 ) . Shakespeare 's day to the Interregnum ( edit ) Shakespeare almost certainly wrote the role of Hamlet for Richard Burbage . He was the chief tragedian of the Lord Chamberlain 's Men , with a capacious memory for lines and a wide emotional range . Judging by the number of reprints , Hamlet appears to have been Shakespeare 's fourth most popular play during his lifetime -- only Henry IV Part 1 , Richard III and Pericles eclipsed it . Shakespeare provides no clear indication of when his play is set ; however , as Elizabethan actors performed at the Globe in contemporary dress on minimal sets , this would not have affected the staging . Firm evidence for specific early performances of the play is scant .","entities":["Shakespeare","Lord Chamberlain's Men","Globe","Maurice Maeterlinck","La Jeune Belgique","Henry IV Part 1","Pericles","Richard Burbage","Richard III","Hamlet"],"facts":["Shakespeare -CREATED-> Ur-Hamlet","Shakespeare -CREATED-> Shakespeare's plays","Shakespeare -CREATED-> Complete Works","Shakespeare -RELATED_TO-> Ur-Hamlet","Shakespeare -RELATED_TO-> Hamnet Shakespeare"]}
{"title":"Hamlet","text":"Hamlet
It was probably one of Shakespeare 's most popular works during his lifetime , and still ranks among his most performed , topping the performance list of the Royal Shakespeare Company and its predecessors in Stratford - upon - Avon since 1879 . It has inspired many other writers -- from Johann Wolfgang von Goethe and Charles Dickens to James Joyce and Iris Murdoch -- and has been described as `` the world 's most filmed story after Cinderella '' . The story of Shakespeare 's Hamlet was derived from the legend of Amleth , preserved by 13th - century chronicler Saxo Grammaticus in his Gesta Danorum , as subsequently retold by the 16th - century scholar François de Belleforest . Shakespeare may also have drawn on an earlier Elizabethan play known today as the Ur - Hamlet , though some scholars believe he himself wrote the Ur - Hamlet , later revising it to create the version of Hamlet we now have . He almost certainly wrote his version of the title role for his fellow actor , Richard Burbage , the leading tragedian of Shakespeare 's time .","entities":["Shakespeare","Royal Shakespeare Company","Stratford-upon-Avon","Johann Wolfgang von Goethe","Charles Dickens","James Joyce","Iris Murdoch","legend of Amleth","Saxo Grammaticus","François de Belleforest","Cinderella","Gesta Danorum","Ur-Hamlet","Richard Burbage","Hamlet"],"facts":["Shakespeare -RELATED_TO-> John Marston","Shakespeare -CREATED-> Shakespeare's plays","Shakespeare -CREATED-> Complete Works","Shakespeare -RELATED_TO-> Hamnet Shakespeare","Shakespeare -RELATED_TO-> works of Francis Bacon"]}
